<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Theoktistos Bryennios</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. 840s</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Theoktistos Bryennios was a Byzantine general and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/strategos">strategos</a> of the theme of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a> in the 840s. Sent by the regency of Empress <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/theodora-wife-of-theophilos">Theodora</a>, he subdued the Slavic peoples of the region, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/melingoi">Melingoi</a> and Ezeritai of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taygetus">Taygetus</a> mountains, who kept their own leaders but had to pay a fixed tribute. The campaign is described in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-vii">Constantine VII</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/de-administrando-imperio">De Administrando Imperio</a>.</p></div>
